# Frontend system

- `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` and semantic CSS variables are the visual source of truth.
- Do not hardcode hex colors, shadows, radii, spacing systems, or typography in components.
- Do not use arbitrary Tailwind values when a semantic token exists.
- Reuse shared primitives before creating a one-off component.
- New components must define default, hover, focus, disabled, loading, error, and success states where applicable.
- Preserve the visual hierarchy: current safety state first, evidence second, action third, technical detail on demand.
- One screen should have one obvious primary action.
- Never hide why an action is unavailable; show the unmet condition.
- Never show an optimistic success state for signing, policy enrollment, transaction submission, or confirmation.
- Always distinguish LIVE, TESTNET, SIMULATED, and FIXTURE states visually and textually.
- Meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, keyboard navigation, visible focus, semantic landmarks, accessible names, and reduced-motion preferences.
- Use plain language before protocol terminology. Put hashes, addresses, raw values, and provider details in expandable technical sections.
- Keep copy calm and precise. Avoid hype, fear language, and unexplained abbreviations.

